# MEM1 at another base (RE4_MEM1_BASE, re4_whole_prelude.h): the GameCube keeps MEM1 at
# 0x80000000, a platform without that address (the 3DS: applications below 0x40000000) moves it.
# - fixed MEM1 addresses (SystemMemInit map, archive load addresses, frame buffers, FIFO,
#   ROM font, DVD buffers) go through RE4_GC
# - the 0x80000000..0x82FFFFFF checks become RE4_IN_MEM1 / bounds from RE4_MEM1_BASE
# - "already relocated" sign tests on file offsets become RE4_IS_ADDR
# - ordering-table entry links (ClearOTagR, its walkers) carry their tag in bit 0 instead of a
#   cleared bit 31, so entries and primitives stay apart below 0x80000000
# - physical to virtual (FST offset, GXGetTexObjData) from RE4_MEM1_BASE
# With the default base every check keeps its GameCube meaning.
